{"entryId":"1403","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1403:1","sourceSha256":"dc80f5efc32b980d15761b0f67734e20d00d7e1dedfd3e1d108f45a0a069954b","englishSha256":"61ba2f5447495ad7484f313f446d4d85d78816785a7506227b49c745f84bbc45","citations":[{"id":"1403:1:citation-01","he":[0,60],"en":[90,100],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_23b.8"},"reference":"Taanit 23b:8","assessment":"The Bavli confirms Choni’s maternal grandson. Ein Yaakov gives Chin(in) and preserves the narrative.","evidence":[{"reference":"Taanit 23b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_23b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Ein Yaakov, Taanit 3:21","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ein_Yaakov%2C_Taanit_3.21"},"witness":"Daat"}]},{"id":"1403:1:citation-02","he":[61,86],"en":[259,280],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Taanit_23b.8.5"},"reference":"Rashi on Taanit 23b:8:5","assessment":"Rashi rejects the explicit privy wording in his preferred reading and explains it for those who have it. Preserve Heilprin’s formulation as reported.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Taanit 23b:8:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Taanit_23b.8.5"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Taanit 23b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_23b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1],"holds":[{"raw":"ובירושלמי כתובות פ\"ב שהיו רוצים למנותו פרנס ולא רצה והחביא עצמו","reason":"Rabbenu Chananel explicitly transmits the proposed appointment and refusal. The cited Jerusalem Ketubot location remains unconfirmed.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rabbeinu Chananel on Taanit 23b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Chananel_on_Taanit_23b.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"raw":"ובעין יעקב בחדושין פי' אחר קבורתו","reason":"Ein Yaakov has the narrative, but the exact Chiddushim comment as described remains unlocated.","evidence":[{"reference":"Ein Yaakov, Taanit 3:21","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ein_Yaakov%2C_Taanit_3.21"},"witness":"Daat"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The Bavli and Ein Yaakov anchor the family and narrative. Rashi distinguishes readings of the privy detail. Rabbenu Chananel independently attests the appointment episode.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Taanit 23b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_23b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Ein Yaakov, Taanit 3:21","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ein_Yaakov%2C_Taanit_3.21"},"witness":"Daat"},{"reference":"Rashi on Taanit 23b:8:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Taanit_23b.8.5"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Rabbeinu Chananel on Taanit 23b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Chananel_on_Taanit_23b.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
